  "category": "historical_issue_fix",
  "description": "### Initial Checks\n\n- [X] I confirm that I'm using Pydantic V2\n\n### Description\n\nIf a type `Annotated` with a custom serialized is using in the definition of a `typing.NamedTuple`, that serializer is not invoked when dumping an instance of the named tuple, even though this works when the same `Annotated` type is used directly via `TypeAdapter`, via a model class, or via a `TypeAdapter` for a regular `tuple`.\r\n\r\nThe attached example defines a `bytes` field that is intended to be converted to a hex `str` when serialized.  For me, the last line of the script fails with an error about `value` including characters that are not legal JSON (or at least I think that's what it's saying), and if I step through with a debugger I can see that the `hex_serialize` function I have is not called in the `NamedTuple` case only.\n\n### Example Code\n\n```Python\nfrom pydantic import PlainSerializer, PlainValidator, TypeAdapter, BaseModel, WithJsonSchema\r\nfrom typing import Annotated, Any, NamedTuple, TypeAlias\r\n\r\n\r\ndef hex_validate(data: Any) -> bytes:\r\n    match data:\r\n        case bytes():\r\n            return data\r\n        case str():\r\n            return bytes.fromhex(data)\r\n        case None:\r\n            return None\r\n\r\n\r\ndef hex_serialize(original: bytes | None) -> str | None:\r\n    if original is None:\r\n        return None\r\n    return original.hex()\r\n\r\n\r\nHexBytes = Annotated[\r\n    bytes,\r\n    PlainValidator(hex_validate),\r\n    PlainSerializer(hex_serialize, return_type=str, when_used=\"always\"),\r\n    WithJsonSchema({\"type\": \"string\"}, mode=\"serialization\"),\r\n]\r\n\r\n\r\nclass ModelWithBytes(BaseModel):\r\n    x: HexBytes\r\n\r\n\r\nTupleWithBytes: TypeAlias = tuple[HexBytes]\r\n\r\n\r\nclass NamedTupleWithBytes(NamedTuple):\r\n    y: HexBytes\r\n\r\n\r\nBYTES_ADAPTER = TypeAdapter(HexBytes)\r\n\r\nTUPLE_ADAPTER = TypeAdapter(TupleWithBytes)\r\n\r\nNAMED_TUPLE_ADAPTER = TypeAdapter(NamedTupleWithBytes)\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    value = b\"\\xe2\\x9f\\xe9\\xf1\\x00\\x8e5\\x9f6\\xa3g~}i\\xccC\\x93v\\xd1\\xe6\"\r\n\r\n    assert BYTES_ADAPTER.validate_json(BYTES_ADAPTER.dump_json(value)) == value\r\n\r\n    a = ModelWithBytes(x=value)\r\n    assert ModelWithBytes.model_validate_json(a.model_dump_json()).x == value\r\n\r\n    b = (value,)\r\n    assert TUPLE_ADAPTER.validate_json(TUPLE_ADAPTER.dump_json(b))[0] == value\r\n\r\n    c = NamedTupleWithBytes(y=value)\r\n    assert NAMED_TUPLE_ADAPTER.validate_json(NAMED_TUPLE_ADAPTER.dump_json(c)).y == value\n```\n\n\n### Python, Pydantic & OS Version\n\n```Text\npydantic version: 2.5.0\r\n        pydantic-core version: 2.14.1\r\n          pydantic-core build: profile=release pgo=false\r\n                 install path: /home/jbosch/LSST/install/conda/envs/lsst-scipipe-7.0.1/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pydantic\r\n               python version: 3.11.4 | packaged by conda-forge | (main, Jun 10 2023, 18:08:17) [GCC 12.2.0]\r\n                     platform: Linux-5.15.0-88-generic-x86_64-with-glibc2.35\r\n             related packages: mypy-1.7.0 typing_extensions-4.8.0\n```\n",
